    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1033">

                <pb facs="0777" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.8273/38d.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister at
                        Mexico City.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department is in receipt of a telegram from the American Consul General at
                    Monterey stating that Vice Consul Silliman is in prison at Saltillo, together
                    with several other American citizens. Please bring this to the attention of the
                    appropriate authorities at once and represent in the strongest possible manner
                    the necessity for immediate action. There can be no possible excuse for the
                    imprisonment of this officer except political antipathy on the part of those
                    responsible for his arrest. The Consul General at Monterey was himself
                    imprisoned for several days prior to the occupation of that <pb facs="0778"
                        n="662" xml:id="pg662"/> city and he was only released when the
                    Constitutionalists took possession of the city. Please insist on immediate
                    action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
